WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:03.564
A fridge notices the milk is running low. An agent orders it and pays.

2
00:00:03.784 --> 00:00:06.344
That took three seconds. The person who has to take it is not home.

3
00:00:06.564 --> 00:00:09.743
A parcel is something you receive at home. That is the assumption we are dropping.

4
00:00:09.963 --> 00:00:13.760
Because nobody lives inside the data. Food, water and medicine have to reach a hand.

5
00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:18.183
Japan ships five billion parcels a year. Last year, eight point three percent were carried twice.

6
00:00:18.403 --> 00:00:22.072
Back when it was one in ten, the government called that sixty thousand drivers of wasted work.

7
00:00:22.292 --> 00:00:26.025
The obvious fixes do not hold. A driverless van still drives back if nobody is home.

8
00:00:26.245 --> 00:00:30.171
Left at the door, it gets taken. And a robot that can open your lock is a way into the house.

9
00:00:30.391 --> 00:00:33.079
So stop making the person wait. Let the parcel follow the person.

10
00:00:33.299 --> 00:00:37.139
Share your location, and the drop point is wherever you are. A store by the station, your office.

11
00:00:37.359 --> 00:00:39.748
Or drop a pin on any street, and the van pulls over right there.

12
00:00:39.968 --> 00:00:43.061
You walk up, and it is yours. No second trip, nothing left on a doorstep.

13
00:00:43.281 --> 00:00:45.265
Delivery OS. Packages adapt to people.
